  "_readme": [
    "Model IDENTITY, CAPABILITY and EXECUTION metadata.",
    "",
    "Deliberately separate from data/model-profiles.json, which is the PROMPT-AUTHORING",
    "registry the compiler consumes: 47 profiles of rules and sections that describe how",
    "to write for a model. This file describes what a model IS, what it can do, and where",
    "it could run. A definition links to a prompt profile by id; it never restates one.",
    "",
    "`id` is the only identity. displayName is a label, and a FAL route is execution",
    "metadata belonging to an adapter - neither may ever be used to select behaviour.",
    "Adding a model must be a data change, never application-wide conditional logic.",
    "",
    "PHASE 1: nothing reads this file at runtime. It is validated by",
    "tests/model-definition-registry.js and consumed by later phases.",
    "",
    "Capability values here are taken from data/model-profiles.json and from official",
    "ComfyUI workflow templates. Where a fact is not established by either, the field is",
    "null or omitted rather than guessed - an invented capability is worse than an absent",
    "one, because something will eventually trust it."
  ],
